Reading of step 1 (written after seeing it):
 - T0. No row dies before the move (T ≥ 1 everywhere): prediction T-d (none at a fixed size) holds;
   "pre-move deaths" are not a cause. But for ω < 0.15, 813 of 1776 rows die within 5 generations of
   the move (273 of 2056 at 0.15–0.3, 14 at 0.3–0.5, none above), never at k < 0.01: there the first
   steps of the optimum (k against ω) kill, a different regime in which a wider ω helps (e_ω > 0).
   Before the move 59% of the population fails viability selection at ω < 0.15 (median), 20% at
   0.15–0.3, 6–9% at 0.3–0.75, under 4% above 0.75.
 - T-a HOLDS, more strongly than predicted. The table's own e_ω inside its low tercile is not one
   number: +0.13 to +0.29 for ω < 0.3 (model A: +0.30 to +0.42 below 0.15), and for ω ≥ 0.3 within
   the tercile −0.51 (L 100), −0.42 (500), −0.37 (1000), −0.20 (5000), se 0.02 (T2, "0.3 ≤ ω"; the
   sub-ranges 0.5 ≤ ω, 1 ≤ ω, 0.5–1.5 agree: −0.50/−0.52, −0.43/−0.51, −0.34/−0.43, −0.15/−0.29).
   The per-bin slopes of T1 scatter around the same values with se of 0.15–0.4 each (too noisy
   one by one; the sub-range fits are the usable summary).
 - T-b HOLDS: 69% of the tercile fit's leverage in log ω (65% at L 5000) sits at ω < 0.3, which
   holds 13% of the tercile's rows and 14–20% of its information. The tercile value −0.14…−0.19 is
   a mixture of a positive branch and a negative branch and is the local elasticity of neither.
 - T3. Phase B's emulator values by bin follow the table's two branches: +0.28 median below 0.15
   (table A +0.35), about 0 at 0.15–0.3, −0.36 at 0.3–0.5, −0.46 to −0.60 from 0.5 to 2.2. Against
   the table's sub-range fits for 0.3 ≤ ω ≤ cut, phase B's cell medians (which are medians of inputs
   mostly in that range) are −0.63 vs −0.51 (L 100), −0.55 vs −0.42 (500), −0.43 vs −0.37 (1000),
   −0.47 vs −0.20 (5000). So T removes most of the "3×": a residual of −0.06 to −0.13 at
   L ≤ 1000 and −0.27 at L = 5000 is left for E.
   The crude leverage re-weighting of the 11–16 sample inputs per cell (last block) gives +0.12,
   +0.01, +0.15, −0.32: it overshoots the table (−0.14…−0.19), i.e. it is dominated by the one or
   two sample inputs below ω = 0.15 and is too noisy to test T-c; the curve of step 2 does that
   properly.
 - Levels: phase B's k50 over the table model's at the same inputs has medians 0.86–1.32 by bin
   with no trend in ω below 2.2 (few inputs per bin).
 - NOT expected (post hoc observation, from phase B's own log and T1/T3 together): for ω of about
   2.2 to 5 the emulator's e_ω is still −0.34 to −0.45 (bin medians) while the table's middle
   tercile is −0.10 to −0.01 (se ≈ 0.05) and its top tercile +0.29 to +0.38. Phase B did not test
   those cells (|table e| < 0.1), but the difference there (about 0.3) is larger than the residual
   in the low tercile. So the emulator's e_ω may turn from negative to positive at a larger ω than
   the table's. This is the candidate residual E; it is outside the "narrow ω" question as posed.

